+   whose cells are ln(1 + scale-tolerance) wide in ln σ and `tol` wide in each offset, or of one of the seven grids
+   shifted from it by half a cell: every copy found agrees within the tolerances, and every set of matches that agrees
+   within half of them falls into one cell of some grid (docs/theory/12 §3). A slide run counts once per copy, however
+   many runs of the note page repeat its string: the matches come grouped by slide run, in order, so a cell has
+   counted run i already exactly when the last run it counted is i. The verdict does not depend on the matches' order,
